Fixed `TXTRecord.text` being limited to 256 characters, which rejected valid records such as 2048-bit DKIM keys. TXT content now follows RFC 1035 §3.3.14: up to 65535 bytes in total, split into `<character-string>` values of up to 255 bytes each. Long values are split automatically, and explicit DNS presentation format (`"part one" "part two"`) is accepted to control where the boundaries fall.
